</span></th>
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dialogue History</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:86.3pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Chosen</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rejected</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Neogotiation and Fluency</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Hello, why is today’s Comfort King Bed Room selling price so high? Could we adjust it to 140 RMB?
<br class="ltx_break">Hotel: No, no—you need a floor for price changes; how could we operate at such a low price?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:86.3pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: I understand your concerns. Nearby hotels are lowering prices; being a bit cheaper is better than losing orders. How about adjusting to 152 RMB?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Then if we adjust to 152 RMB, is that okay?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Neogotiation and Fluency</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Our hotel’s order conversion has been quite low recently. Could we adjust today’s Comfort King Bed Room price to 83 RMB?
<br class="ltx_break">Hotel: No, that’s too low. Would there be any profit left for me?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:86.3pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Of course there would—please don’t joke. How about we adjust it to 90 RMB?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Then let’s set it to 90 RMB, okay?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Process Compilance</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Hello, can we lower tomorrow’s Deluxe Room price to 109 RMB? 
<br class="ltx_break">Hotel: No—how could we run business at that price? 
<br class="ltx_break">BD: Don’t say that; I’m trying to bring more orders to the hotel. Let’s not change today’s price then. 
<br class="ltx_break">Hotel: Right, don’t change it without permission. 
<br class="ltx_break">BD: Okay, then can we adjust tomorrow’s Special Offer King Room to 116 RMB? 
<br class="ltx_break">Hotel: Tomorrow’s can be adjusted.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:86.3pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Great, I’ll set tomorrow’s Special Offer King Room to 116 RMB; no other adjustments. Goodbye.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Okay, I won’t bother you then. Goodbye.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Guardrail Phrasing</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Hello, why is today’s Special Offer Twin Room’s price so high? Could we adjust it to 97 RMB to boost orders? 
<br class="ltx_break">Hotel: No, no—that price is too low.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:86.3pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Then how about 105 RMB?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">BD: Then shall I set it to the work-order targeted price of 105 RMB?</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Preference data examples illustrating negotiation and fluency, process compliance, and guardrail phrasing.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Task challenges and REPO solutions.</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section outlines the core challenges in OTA price negotiation—persuasion, SOP adherence, business numerics, guardrails, and formatting—and how REPO targets each with the right reward source. As summarized in Table <a href="#A2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix B Task challenges and REPO solutions. ‣ Teaching LLM to be Persuasive: Reward-Enhanced Policy Optimization for Alignment from Heterogeneous Rewards" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, REPO uses a tri-source design: the reward model (RM) provides dense supervision to learn human BD tactics and SOP patterns; the reward judge (RJ) applies rubric-based assessments to enforce nuanced behaviors (e.g., emotional value, progress tracking, avoiding over-negotiation or scope creep); and programmatic reward functions (RF) supply deterministic checks for verifiable requirements (numerical consistency, schema/format, language use, CoT leakage, repetition, and length). RJ and RF modulate the RM via stability-preserving enhancement, reducing reward hacking while preserving training stability. This separation of concerns keeps subjective persuasion and process judgments (RM/RJ) distinct from auditable constraints (RF), enables fast iteration by editing judge prompts, and ensures coverage of long-horizon failure modes—for example, accepting favorable counteroffers, not inferring consent from silence, matching price types to room/date, and preventing output formats that break downstream systems.</p>
</div>
